{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3FUb9GxX7eEtkmBUSMj","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't changed anything, because per-day rows can't fit in `out/summary.csv`. The README says the partner portal silently cuts the file off after 50 lines, and 2025 has up to 365 days of transactions. The portal would keep only the first month and a half or so and report no error. Adding columns instead doesn't work either, since the portal rejects anything other than `period,total,count`.\n\nSome options:\n\n- **A separate file**, e.g. `out/summary_daily.csv`, also `period,total,count` but with `period` as `2025-12-06`. The monthly summary stays as it is. This is what I'd do, but only if the portal or partner can take a second file, or you can send it another way. I don't know if they can.\n- **Coarser periods in the existing file**, e.g. weekly (about 52 rows, still too many) or monthly plus quarterly. That stays under the limit but isn't per-day.\n- **Ask the partner** how they want to receive the daily data, given the 50-line limit.\n\nWhich do you want?\n\nSeparately, `out/summary.csv` is out of date. It has 11 months and is missing the December data I committed earlier, because nobody has run `scripts/summarize.py` since then. Want me to regenerate it?","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":502,"cache_read_input_tokens":16990,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":502,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-30>","timestamp":"2026-11-14T17:55:27.959Z","request_id":"gen-1794678921-a9Fdf9ltjwcir8wXxSZ3"}
